[71.524681, "o", "Help on function input in module bytewax.operators:\r\n\r\ninput(step_id: str, flow: bytewax.dataflow.Dataflow, source: bytewax.inputs.Source[~X]) -> bytewax.dataflow.Stream[~X]\r\n    Introduce items into a dataflow.\r\n\r\n    ```{testcode}\r\n    from bytewax.dataflow import Dataflow\r\n    import bytewax.operators as op\r\n    from bytewax.testing import TestingSource\r\n\r\n    flow = Dataflow(\"input_eg\")\r\n    nums = op.input(\"nums\", flow, TestingSource([10, 20, 30]))\r\n    op.inspect(\"out\", nums)\r\n    ```\r\n\r\n    ```{testcode}\r\n    :hide:\r\n"]
[71.524731, "o", "    from bytewax.testing import run_main\r\n\r\n    run_main(flow)\r\n    ```\r\n\r\n    ```{testoutput}\r\n    input_eg.out: 10\r\n    input_eg.out: 20\r\n    input_eg.out: 30\r\n    ```\r\n\r\n    See {py:obj}`bytewax.inputs` for more information on how input\r\n    works. See {py:obj}`bytewax.connectors` for a buffet of our\r\n"]
[71.534764, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@2eacb342-88a4-4e90-86f7-a5580b74af48:~# "]
[72.174661, "i", "python3 -c 'import bytewax.operators as op; help(op.output)' 2>&1 | head -30\n"]
[72.175096, "o", "python3 -c 'import bytewax.operators as op; help(op.output)' 2>&1 | head -30\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[72.262952, "o", "Help on function output in module bytewax.operators:\r\n\r\noutput(step_id: str, up: bytewax.dataflow.Stream[~X], sink: bytewax.outputs.Sink[~X]) -> None\r\n    Write items out of a dataflow.\r\n\r\n    ```{testcode}\r\n    from bytewax.dataflow import Dataflow\r\n    import bytewax.operators as op\r\n    from bytewax.testing import TestingSource\r\n    from bytewax.connectors.stdio import StdOutSink\r\n\r\n    flow = Dataflow(\"output_eg\")\r\n    nums = op.input(\"nums\", flow, TestingSource([1, 2, 3]))\r\n\r\n    # This will print the items to stdout.\r\n    # You can replace this with any other sink.\r\n    op.output(\"sink\", nums, StdOutSink())\r\n    ```\r\n\r\n    ```{testcode}\r\n    :hide:\r\n\r\n    from bytewax.testing import run_main\r\n\r\n"]
[72.263035, "o", "    run_main(flow)\r\n    ```\r\n\r\n    ```{testoutput}\r\n    1\r\n    2\r\n"]
